Z||000000||stimpy||03-10-2000||11:12 PM||||Well, in 12 hours I'm on a plane back to the foodbasket of the world, the Big Valley, good ol' Central Valley of California. I will be visiting my folks and helping with the Fiero show that will be part of the festivities of my dads tire store.  I know a bunch of you folks have made plans to join us and I am really looking forward to meeting y'all. We've got some big plans to mae it a fun gathering for all involved.  I will be checking in from my dads computer so if anyone has any last minute ?'s please post or email to Big O.<BR>PS, It is snowing on Oklahoma City tonight... California here I come!!!!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-10-2000||11:29 PM||||Stimpy, My door is open, if you hit the San Francisco bay area look me up. I'll be at your dads Friday the 17th. I think this is going to be a great Fiero Event. I know your dad started the detailing of his car?? if I start washing and waxing today maybe the little black toy will be clean by the 18th <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>see ya there!||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||03-11-2000||12:11 AM||||Thanks for the invite- You live in South City right? We definately want to get some touring in, but Bay Area traffic freaks me out (grew up in San Jo- Go Sharks!) Probably more likely going to be going up TerryK's way. I am gonna beg nd wheedle and whine to see if Pops will let me borrow the Red Rocket to drive up Highway 49. It's been so long since I've driven on a road that curves... Then again Skyline Boulevard is a nice little trip too!<BR> Anyways.. I'll have plenty of detailing goodies on hand. I talked to my mom the other night and found out that my dad is putting me in charge of judging the show otherwise I'd be happy to give a helping hand puttg the finishing touches on your ride. Is DXR_MOM bringin out Code21?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||03-11-2000||01:48 AM||||I would love to have both my cars there <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but code21 won't be making this trip. Skyline ? the old street race road. I did 2yrs at Skyline College Auto Tech. I know that road well. For a while Hillside Blvd. was the spot but homes are going up all over So.SF <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> to bad for the street racers?? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">not much left out here. Brotherhood way back in the late 70's......Ah the good old days!! ||||reg||1
